<h2 id="article-changes">See what changed in an article</h2>
<ol><li>Save a checkpoint before revising your article.</li><li>Edit, then open Revisions in this tab and choose the saved version you want to compare.</li><li>Open Article changes. Removed lines come from the saved article; added lines come from the current article. Labels include their line numbers. Unchanged lines are omitted.</li><li>Use Field to compare below it when you need the complete text, metadata, source notes, or review questions. A matching article body does not mean every workspace field matches.</li></ol>
<p>The comparison includes blank lines, line endings, and a missing final line break. A paragraph written on one long line appears as a whole changed line. This is a text comparison, not a word-by-word explanation, a merge, a fact-check, or an export-approval decision. A moved section can appear as removed and added writing.</p>
<p>Only the first forty change groups are displayed. Each passage initially shows at most eight lines or 800 characters. A shortened-preview notice and Show complete saved/current passage control let you read the complete change. Large changed regions may be grouped to keep processing bounded, with a visible notice that matching lines inside them can also appear as added and removed. The complete versions also remain in the saved/current fields. The comparison updates after edits or checkpoint selection, and clearing the workspace removes its temporary text. It is excluded from backups and article exports and makes no upload or AI request.</p>
